<small>A Song of degrees.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say:<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> The LORD <i>is</i> righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Let them be as the grass <i>upon</i> the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD <i>be</i> upon you: we bless you in the name of the LORD. <br />
